// Obfusku Canonical Example: Mutable Cells and Rebinding
//
// Demonstrates:
// 1. Declaring top-level mutable cells using `≔˚`.
// 2. Rebinding mutable cells with `⚙︎`.
// 3. Capturing mutable cells in closures via explicit capture sigil `˚`.
// 4. Local mutable bindings chained with LocalBinding syntax.

// Top-level mutable cell
counter ≔˚ 10

// A closure explicitly capturing 'counter' to mutate it in place
λbump(step: ⟁): ∅ → ˚counter ⚙︎ counter ✚ step

// Invoke the closure to mutate the captured cell
step1 ≔ bump(15)
step2 ≔ bump(25)

// Local mutable cell demonstration:
// Local bindings take the form `name ≔ expr \n continuation`.
// Because `x ⚙︎ val` evaluates to Unit (∅), we bind it to a discard name.
localCalculation ≔ (
  x ≔˚ 5
  discard ≔ x ⚙︎ x ✱ 4
  x
)

// The final result combines top-level mutated counter (50) and local cell (20)
result ≔ counter ✚ localCalculation
❧
